1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,122
You tell yourself just one more video, and suddenly it's 1am.

2
00:00:04,442 --> 00:00:11,629
There's a name for that: revenge bedtime procrastination, and a recent national survey found most American adults do it regularly.

3
00:00:11,949 --> 00:00:15,755
Scrolling delays melatonin with blue light, and diet makes it worse.

4
00:00:16,075 --> 00:00:22,779
Two out of three American adults don't get enough magnesium, so your nervous system stays wired even after the phone's down.

5
00:00:23,099 --> 00:00:26,632
Three foods may help: kiwi, pistachios, and warm milk.

6
00:00:26,952 --> 00:00:33,732
Research suggests two kiwis about an hour before bed can help you fall asleep faster and sleep longer.

7
00:00:34,052 --> 00:00:38,265
Pistachios naturally contain melatonin, tryptophan, and magnesium.

8
00:00:38,585 --> 00:00:45,984
Warm milk isn't just an old story either — casein peptides formed as milk digests have a calming effect on the nervous system.

9
00:00:46,304 --> 00:00:54,020
These foods won't fix bedtime procrastination alone, but paired with a set phone cutoff, falling asleep gets a lot easier.
